(>> 5.3 Technical Punctuation Standards) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Semicolon \(;\): Links two independent clauses that are closely connected in meaning) Tj
T*
(without a coordinating conjunction. Also separates complex list items containing) Tj
T*
(internal commas:) Tj
T*
("The samples were collected from three locations: Jalandhar, Punjab; Shimla, Himachal) Tj
T*
(Pradesh; and Srinagar, Kashmir.") Tj
T*
(* Colon \(:\): Introduces formal lists, explanations, or long quotations. Must follow a) Tj
T*
(grammatically complete independent clause \(Never place a colon directly after a verb) Tj
T*
(like 'are:' or 'consists of:'\).) Tj
T*
(* Hyphen \(-\) vs. En-Dash \(--\) vs. Em-Dash \(---\):) Tj
T*
(- Hyphen: Joins compound adjectives preceding nouns: "a low-molecular-weight) Tj
T*
(peptide", "water-soluble polymer".) Tj
T*
(- En-Dash: Expresses numerical ranges: "pages 45--52", "temperature 37--42 deg C".) Tj
T*
(- Em-Dash: Sets off an abrupt parenthetical emphasis or clarification within a) Tj
T*
(sentence.) Tj
T*
(* Apostrophe \('\): Denotes possession \(the bacterium's membrane; the bacteria's) Tj
T*
(membranes\) or contraction. Never used to form plurals \(*DNA's is strictly) Tj
T*
(ungrammatical for plural DNAs\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 1: Active to Passive Transformation of Laboratory Protocols]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Convert the following active voice laboratory procedures into formal academic) Tj
T*
(passive voice, eliminating informal personal pronouns \(I, we, you\):) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "We measured 50 mL of nutrient broth using a graduated cylinder and poured) Tj
T*
(it into an Erlenmeyer flask.") Tj
T*
(- Passive Transformation: "Fifty milliliters of nutrient broth was measured using) Tj
T*
(a graduated cylinder and poured into an Erlenmeyer flask.") Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "The researcher has calibrated the pH meter using standard buffer solutions) Tj
T*
(at pH 4.0, 7.0, and 10.0.") Tj
T*
(- Passive Transformation: "The pH meter has been calibrated using standard buffer) Tj
T*
(solutions at pH 4.0, 7.0, and 10.0.") Tj
T*
(Sentence 3: "The laboratory team is monitoring the dissolved oxygen concentration inside) Tj
T*
(the fermenter continuously.") Tj
T*
(- Passive Transformation: "The dissolved oxygen concentration inside the fermenter) Tj
T*
(is being monitored continuously.") Tj
T*
(Sentence 4: "You must autoclave all surgical dissection tools at 121 deg C for twenty) Tj
T*
(minutes.") Tj
T*
(- Passive Transformation: "All surgical dissection tools must be autoclaved at 121) Tj
T*
(deg C for twenty minutes.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 2: Modal Selection for Scientific Hedging]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Select the appropriate modal verb \(must, should, may, might\) to match the) Tj
T*
(specified degree of scientific certainty:) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1 \(Degree of Certainty: Weak Speculative Possibility ~20%\):) Tj
T*
("The unexpected peak observed at 260 nm [must / should / might] correspond to trace) Tj
T*
(amounts of residual nucleic acid contamination.") Tj
T*
ET

endstream
