(- Selected Modal: MIGHT. \(Reflects cautious academic hedging\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 2 \(Degree of Certainty: High Expected Probability ~80%\):) Tj
T*
("Based on thermodynamic calculations, the biological reaction [must / should / might]) Tj
T*
(attain steady state within fifteen minutes.") Tj
T*
(- Selected Modal: SHOULD. \(Expresses reasoned expectation from theory\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 3 \(Degree of Certainty: Logical Certainty / Inescapable Fact >95%\):) Tj
T*
("Because the control plates devoid of ampicillin supported extensive bacterial growth,) Tj
T*
(the antibiotic batch [must / should / might] be fully functional.") Tj
T*
(- Selected Modal: MUST. \(Expresses logical deduction based on control evidence\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 3: Punctuation Remediation in Complex Technical Sentences]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Punctuate the following unpunctuated academic paragraph correctly using) Tj
T*
(semicolons, colons, hyphens, and commas:) Tj
T*
(Unpunctuated Draft:) Tj
T*
("the research team analyzed three distinct bio fuels namely ethanol derived from) Tj
T*
(sugarcane bio diesel from jatropha seeds and bio hydrogen from cyanobacteria however the) Tj
T*
(production yields varied significantly ethanol achieved high efficiency bio diesel) Tj
T*
(exhibited moderate stability and bio hydrogen produced negligible quantities") Tj
T*
(Fully Punctuated Academic Version:) Tj
T*
("The research team analyzed three distinct bio-fuels, namely: ethanol derived from) Tj
T*
(sugarcane, bio-diesel from jatropha seeds, and bio-hydrogen from cyanobacteria. However,) Tj
T*
(the production yields varied significantly; ethanol achieved high efficiency, bio-diesel) Tj
T*
(exhibited moderate stability, and bio-hydrogen produced negligible quantities.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 4: Hyphenation of Compound Technical Adjectives]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Apply hyphens to compound adjectives only where grammatically required:) Tj
T*
(1. A well documented protocol -> A well-documented protocol. \(Preceding noun\).) Tj
T*
(2. The protocol is well documented -> The protocol is well documented. \(Predicate) Tj
T*
(position; NO hyphen\).) Tj
T*
(3. High performance liquid chromatography -> High-performance liquid chromatography.) Tj
T*
(4. Highly active biological catalyst -> Highly active biological catalyst. \(Adverbs) Tj
T*
(ending in -ly NEVER take hyphens\).) Tj
T*
(5. State of the art instrumentation -> State-of-the-art instrumentation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.4 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Explain why the passive voice is predominantly favored in the Materials and) Tj
T*
(Methods section of experimental research papers.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Passive voice is preferred in scientific reporting because: \(1\) Objectivity and) Tj
T*
(Impersonality: Science values reproducible methodology over personal agency. Phrasing) Tj
T*
(procedures as 'The cells were harvested at 4 deg C' emphasizes the standardized physical) Tj
T*
(action rather than who performed it \('I harvested the cells'\). \(2\) Focus on the) Tj
T*
(Recipient of Action: The biological specimen, reagent, or apparatus is the rightful) Tj
T*
(focal subject of the study; placing it in the grammatical subject position centers the) Tj
T*
(reader's attention on the scientific variable. \(3\) Universality and Replicability:) Tj
T*
ET

