(Stating that 'The medium was autoclaved for 20 minutes' frames the protocol as an) Tj
T*
(invariant procedural standard that any competent researcher globally can replicate with) Tj
T*
(identical results.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Contrast the grammatical and functional usage of the Semicolon \(;\), Colon \(:\),) Tj
T*
(and Em-Dash \(---\) in academic prose.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) Semicolon \(;\): Structurally links two independent clauses that share close) Tj
T*
(semantic and thematic affinity without relying on coordinating conjunctions: 'The) Tj
T*
(initial velocity was recorded; the data followed Michaelis-Menten kinetics.' Also used) Tj
T*
(as a super-comma in complex lists containing internal commas. \(2\) Colon \(:\): Directs) Tj
T*
(attention forward to introduce an elaboration, explanation, or enumerated list. The) Tj
T*
(clause preceding a colon must be an independent sentence: 'The assay requires three) Tj
T*
(reagents: buffer, enzyme, and substrate.' \(3\) Em-Dash \(---\): Creates an emphatic, abrupt) Tj
T*
(rhetorical break to set off parenthetical insights or dramatic summaries: 'The entire) Tj
T*
(batch---despite multiple sterilization cycles---showed fungal contamination.') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.5 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Passive voice \(be + V3\) prioritizes experimental procedures over human actors in) Tj
T*
(scientific reports.) Tj
T*
(* Modals reflect epistemic probability: must \(>95%\), should \(~80%\), may \(~50%\), might) Tj
T*
(\(<30%\).) Tj
T*
(* Semicolons link related independent clauses; colons introduce lists after complete) Tj
T*
(sentences.) Tj
T*
(* Hyphens connect compound adjectives preceding nouns; adverbs ending in -ly never) Tj
T*
(take hyphens.) Tj
T*
